# (the voices batch, item 2) Pluck, a plucked string, on both sequences' ALGORITHM: the Sequence's sixth voice (after
# Glass), Sequence 2's seventh (after Sub, which keeps its place); said, kept in the project, its page shown with it,
# heard (its strings struck as Skellig plays), and kept over a restart. (AISLING, step 4) The voices appended after it:
# the Sequence's Bouzouki and Dulcimer (one turn back from 2600), Sequence 2's Bouzouki, Dulcimer and Bodhran
wait 300
listen
tap ARP
wait 300
expect view 2
# (AISLING) Skellig's harp is this voice already (Pluck, renamed Harp, its ring made long, 2026-10-30): one turn back
# is Glass, one on Harp again
expect par33 5
turn ALGO -1
wait 300
said VOICE Glass
expect par33 4
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE Harp
expect par33 5
tap ARP
wait 300
expect view 9
said Seq sound page, voice Harp: Cutoff 55, Decay 80, Reverb 50, Echo 50
shot seqpluck.png
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE Bouzouki
expect par33 6
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE Dulcimer
expect par33 7
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE Patch
expect par33 8
turn ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE 2600
expect par33 0
turn ALGO -2
wait 300
said VOICE Dulcimer
expect par33 7
turn ALGO -2
wait 300
said VOICE Harp
expect par33 5
tap SEQ
wait 300
expect view 4
spin ALGO -2
wait 300
said VOICE Patch
expect par35 10
spin ALGO -1
wait 300
said VOICE Bodhran
expect par35 9
spin ALGO 2
wait 300
said VOICE 2600
expect par35 0
spin ALGO -2
wait 300
said VOICE Bodhran
expect par35 9
spin ALGO -3
wait 300
said VOICE Harp
expect par35 6
spin ALGO -1
wait 300
said VOICE Sub
expect par35 5
spin ALGO 1
wait 300
said VOICE Harp
expect par35 6
wait 8000
expect ksstruck >0
# kept: stopped, it saves itself; the same after a restart (the save's format AISLING's own, now 3; Pluck and step 4's
# voices appended, nothing moved)
tap PLAY
wait 6000
expect dirty 0
expect store_writes >0
reboot
wait 500
expect format 3
expect par33 5
expect par35 6
